# The private corpus: observed incidents, captured by `cairn capture`.
#
# CLAUDE.md §3 — raw producer output, hand-redacted output, and the event streams
# derived from them never reach this repository. Only the taxonomy built from
# them and the accuracy measured over them are published.
#
# This is the weakest of the three guards, because `git add -f` steps over it.
# scripts/pre-commit refuses the staging, and scripts/check-boundary.sh asserts
# nothing observed is tracked — that one runs in CI, on GitHub, so it catches a
# bypass of the other two.
/corpus/

# Site-local configuration: generated per deployment, never committed upstream.
# `cairn init` writes this; admins review and commit it in THEIR repo, not ours.
site.yaml
policy.yaml
*.local.*
*.local

